From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:25:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77705: Take the charge current from the
 battery

The chip comes up limiting the charge to 450 mA, which is a safe value for
a cell nobody described and a needlessly slow one for a cell that is.  The
driver already asks for the battery description and uses its end-of-charge
voltage, so use the current from it as well; the limit of what the supply
on the other end can deliver is a separate property and stays untouched.

Measured on a Galaxy S10+, whose cell is described as taking 2850 mA: the
charger reports 900 mA before this change and 2850 mA after it, without
anyone writing to sysfs.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
index 63b0b4f0cd2..c7eff705a14 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
@@ -528,7 +528,23 @@ static int max77705_charger_initialize(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 	if (err)
 		goto err;
 
-	/* charge current 450mA(default) */
+	/*
+	 * Charge current: the chip comes up at 450 mA, which is a safe value
+	 * for a cell nobody described and a needlessly slow one for a cell
+	 * that is.  The battery node states what the cell takes, so use it;
+	 * what the supply on the other end can deliver is a separate limit
+	 * and stays where it is.
+	 */
+	if (info->constant_charge_current_max_ua > 0) {
+		err = max77705_set_integer(chg, MAX77705_CHG_CC_LIM,
+					   MAX77705_CURRENT_CHGIN_MIN,
+					   MAX77705_CURRENT_CHGIN_MAX,
+					   MAX77705_CURRENT_CHG_STEP,
+					   info->constant_charge_current_max_ua);
+		if (err)
+			goto err;
+	}
+
 	/* otg current limit 900mA */
 	err = regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_OTG_ILIM], MAX77705_OTG_ILIM_900);
 	if (err)
